185
00:08:38.799 --> 00:08:41.010
No, no, no, at the end of my senior year,

186
00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.430
I was closer to about 300.

187
00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:45.830
What did you weigh in high school?

188
00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:49.270
In high school I flipped, I went from about 280,

189
00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.500
my sophomore year up to about 295 my senior year.

190
00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.333
Holy smokes.

191
00:08:53.333 --> 00:08:54.880
So were you just a big kid,

192
00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.609
or, like, how did you put so much weight on?

193
00:08:56.609 --> 00:08:57.599
How tall are you?

194
00:08:57.599 --> 00:08:59.850
It's just natural, I'm 6'4" now.

195
00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:04.850
I was 6'2", 6'3" in that area in high school, yeah.

196
00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.710
Uh-huh, were you one of those kids

197
00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.328
who was just always the biggest, strongest kid in the class?

198
00:09:09.328 --> 00:09:11.880
Right, yeah, I was always the big kid,

199
00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.770
and my grandfather was a big man.

200
00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:18.770
I come from big people, and my grandmother kept us heavy.

201
00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.815
What was it like when you were growing up?

202
00:09:21.815 --> 00:09:24.280
Like, what was the typical meal in the house,

203
00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.270
or what was a day in the life of food for you?

204
00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:28.440
Oh, my goodness.

205
00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.890
Well, my grandfather owned a construction business,

206
00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:36.413
and I spent a lot of time spending a night with them,

207
00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.200
and getting up to go to work in the morning.

208
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:44.020
Now, what we would do before anybody ever got up,

209
00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.720
what woke us up was the smell of bacon in the morning,

210
00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.780
and my grandmother cooking biscuits.

211
00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:52.846
And so we had bacon, biscuits, and gravy,

212
00:09:52.846 --> 00:09:56.460
the standard scrambled eggs.

213
00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.940
She did these awesome fig preserves.

214
00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.600
She made all of these different things.

215
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.380
And so every meal in the house throughout the day

216
00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.280
was a completely one-off meal,

217
00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:09.180
brand new, fresh cooked, hot meal, breakfast.

218
00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.000
We came home for lunch and it was a hot meal for lunch.

219
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.870
And the same thing for supper.

220
00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.710
And we had snacks all in between.

221
00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.030
It was all about food,

222
00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:20.190
and the food was the love in their mind.

223
00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:24.160
They come from more meager beginnings.

224
00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.844
And I feel like a lot of their agrarian, like, background,

225
00:10:28.844 --> 00:10:32.770
and the Depression,

226
00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.170
Arab folks,

227
00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:37.590
I feel like they really kind of overcompensate with food

228
00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.220
because they had so little back then,

229
00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.150
and they want to make sure

230
00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.514
that the people they're taking care of

231
00:10:41.514 --> 00:10:45.800
really understand how much they love them via food.

232
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:46.633
Right.

233
00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:48.020
I feel like that happens a lot, you know?

234
00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:48.853
Right, right.

235
00:10:48.853 --> 00:10:51.320
Do you have brothers and sisters?

236
00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.470
Yeah, I sure do.

237
00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.305
Uh-huh, so how many of those?

238
00:10:54.305 --> 00:10:56.264
I have a younger brother

239
00:10:56.264 --> 00:10:59.910
who is about 2-1/2 years younger than I am.

240
00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.823
Also was a football player, also a big man.

241
00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:10.410
By the way, he to date is down almost 150 pounds.

242
00:11:11.249 --> 00:11:12.082
Wow.

243
00:11:12.082 --> 00:11:15.040
Since he's followed me along

244
00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.370
'cause when I first brought it up as an idea,

245
00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.150
he's like, "Dude, really?

246
00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.290
You're gonna give up meat, and crawfish.

247
00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:25.240
and you're gonna give up fish?"

248
00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.640
And, I mean, it just blew his mind, you know?

249
00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.473
Uh-huh.

250
00:11:28.473 --> 00:11:29.920
I said, give me 30 days and watch me.

251
00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.130
Just give me 30 days.

252
00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.117
And we did it that way and it worked out.

253
00:11:33.117 --> 00:11:35.873
And so my little sister same boat.

254
00:11:38.106 --> 00:11:42.610
My little sister is about five years younger

255
00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:43.830
than my little brother,

256
00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.175
so about 7-1/2 years younger than me.

257
00:11:46.175 --> 00:11:50.740
She's a lot shorter than we are.

258
00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.820
We're both big stature fellows,

259
00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.810
like, we take after my grandfather,

260
00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.740
who's the patriarch of our family.

261
00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:04.193
And he was 6'3" in the high 300s my whole life.

262
00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.560
